face-image: img/campaign.jpg

= [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] Reformation

As the newly elected chairman of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], Adam Sedgewick has been working to expand the party's reach in Protestant areas and quell opposition against his agenda. As a trade union leader himself, he has sizable influence over the Christian labor movement, which is already well-connected through entrenched network of alliances with various right-wing organizations. [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": Cooperation between the various Christian labor unions have been heightened, and together, they are taking down our long-held dominance over the interests of the working-class. ?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": However, Mallin of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> maintains strict oversight of its <span style="color: #6D5298;">Christian Social</span> wing, and will not tolerate any cooperation, making the process considerably more challenging without support of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> affiliated unions. Furthermore, Mallin's inaction as the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> loses its main voter base is fueling significant internal turmoil over the party's future direction. ?]

This has led to concerns from the labor wing of our party, as we can't afford to lose support of the largest demographic to the propertied.

- @fightback_working: We will increase our campaigning towards the working class.
- @fightback_other: We will increase our campaigning towards other demographics to compensate.
- @nothing: Unfortunate.

@fightback_working
subtitle: -2 resources.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle:[? if resources < 2 : We do not have enough resources. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 2; commons_marcher += 8; disfavored_marcher += 5; commons_collectivist += 1; burgher_marcher += 4; labor_dissent -= 10

We increase our messaging among the workers, fighting back against the shift to the right. It isn't enough, but it is something. 

@fightback_other
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: -1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle:[? if resources < 1 : We do not have enough resources. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 1; commons_collectivist += 5; burgher_marcher += 6; guild_marcher += 4; landed_marcher += 4; faithful_marcher += 4; labor_dissent += 15; left_dissent += 10; zentrum_disintegration += 1; peoples_party_support += 1; liberal_cooperation += 2

If the propertied wants to appeal to the workers, then we will simply find support elsewhere. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> makes inroads on our inaction. The left of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> is opposed to this path, seeing it as diluting the class character of the party. On the other hand, reformists support branching out to different classes.

@nothing
on-arrival: zentrum_disintegration += 1; 

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] continues to eat into our party's primary voter base.